      "text": "The root cause is that `EstimatorV2` only accepts Pauli-based observables (`SparsePauliOp` or Pauli strings), not a general `Operator`. I convert the operator to a `SparsePauliOp` with `from_operator`, which decomposes any Hermitian matrix into Pauli terms, and add the import it needs.\n\n```python\nfrom math import pi\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit, transpile\n# FIX: SparsePauliOp was not imported -> added it to the quantum_info import, because the observable must be converted to a SparsePauliOp for EstimatorV2\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import Operator, SparsePauliOp\nfrom qiskit_aer import AerSimulator\nfrom qiskit_ibm_runtime import EstimatorV2\n\nbackend = AerSimulator()\nestimator = EstimatorV2(mode=backend)\n\nO = Operator([[1,0,0,-2j],\n              [0,0,0,0],\n              [0,0,0,0],\n              [2j,0,0,1]])\n\n# FIX: EstimatorV2 rejects a raw Operator observable -> convert it to a SparsePauliOp via from_operator, because it decomposes the matrix into Pauli terms the Estimator accepts\nobs = SparsePauliOp.from_operator(O)\n\nqc = QuantumCircuit(2)\nqc.rx(pi/3,1)\nqc.cx(1,0)\n\nqc_t = transpile(qc,backend)\n\njob = estimator.run([(qc_t,[obs])])\nexp_vals = job.result()[0].data.evs\nprint(exp_vals)\n```",
